### Table of Errors and Fixes:

| Error Type                  | Original Code Behavior                                  | Debugged Code Behavior                                                                 |
| :-------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------ | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Memory Leak**             | Memory for all but the first element was never freed. | All allocated memory is correctly deallocated.                                         |
| **Incorrect Deallocation**  | `delete` used on an array (`new[]`).                    | `delete[]` used for array deallocation.                                                |
| **Undefined Behavior**      | Potential crashes, data corruption due to incorrect `delete`. | Safe deallocation, preventing undefined behavior.                                        |
| **Exception Handling**      | No explicit handling for allocation failure.            | `try-catch` block gracefully handles `std::bad_alloc` and other potential exceptions. |
| **Dangling Pointers**       | Pointer remained after `delete` (if it wasn't leaked). | Pointer is set to `nullptr` after deallocation.                                        |

